# Lazynext Slop Guard (Cursor rules)

Company: Lazynext · UNITED GLOBAL VENTURES PRIVATE LIMITED · support@lazynext.com · https://lazynext.com

## When this applies

You are editing or reviewing prose, product copy, docs, or UI markup that a
model (or a hurried human) may have written. Before calling it done, check it
against the tells below. Every tell is a *default nobody chose* — a deliberate
choice is not slop and must be preserved.

## Writing tells — cut or fix

1. **Banned vocabulary.** Remove or replace: delve, foster, leverage, utilize,
   facilitate, empower, streamline, robust, cutting-edge, paradigm shift,
   game-changer, tapestry, realm, beacon, multifaceted, meticulous, intricate,
   paramount, transformative, elevate, embark, supercharge, harness,
   ever-evolving, seamless, unlock, journey, synergy, next-level,
   revolutionize. Name the mechanism instead.
2. **Empty phrases.** Delete: "it's worth noting", "it's important to note",
   "at the end of the day", "at its core", "in today's world", "in the age of",
   "in the world of", "the reality is", "the truth is", "when it comes to",
   "in terms of", "with regard to", "in order to", "going forward", "let's
   dive in", "it turns out".
3. **Throat-clearing / faux insight.** Delete: "here's the thing",
   "let me be clear", "i'll be honest", "the uncomfortable truth is", "what
   nobody tells you", "what most people get wrong", "the part everyone
   misses". State the claim directly.
4. **Rhythm crutches.** Binary contrasts ("It's not X. It's Y."), colon
   reveals ("The best part: it learns."), negative listings ("Not a X. Not a
   Y. A Z."), dramatic fragments ("X. And Y. And Z."), em-dash clusters
   (3+ dashes), stacked one-liners. Rewrite as plain, varied prose.
5. **Puffery and weasel words.** "stands as a testament", "marks a pivotal
   moment", "plays a vital role", "experts agree", "studies show" — cut or
   cite. Empty adverbs (really, just, literally, genuinely, simply, actually,
   truly, fundamentally, importantly, crucially, inherently, inevitably,
   arguably) — cut when they add nothing.
6. **Formatting slop.** Emoji in headings, decorative bold, bullets where
   prose belongs, headers over two-sentence sections.

## Design tells — UI in this diff

1. **Colour:** indigo-violet gradients (`from-indigo-500 to-violet-600`,
   `#6366f1`→`#a855f7`), gradient headline text (`bg-clip-text
   text-transparent`), colored glow shadows, warm amber/stone "cozy" washes
   applied everywhere.
2. **Type:** one serif-italic word inside a sans headline, display serifs
   (Playfair/Lora/Cormorant) in UI, a tracked-caps kicker above every heading
   (`uppercase tracking-widest`), h1 at `text-lg`/`text-base` (flat
   hierarchy), default Inter/Space Grotesk pairings with no stated reason.
3. **Components:** `animate-ping` status dots, `border-l-4` callouts on every
   list item, rounded-square icon tiles, `backdrop-blur` glass surfaces,
   `rounded-full` pills on cards, badge/pill spam ("✨ New", "β Beta"),
   `bg-blue-50` icon-in-a-tint-of-itself, huge soft drop shadows, "Powered by
   AI" badges.
4. **Motion:** `hover:scale-105` + `transition-all` on everything, spinners
   whose rotate keyframe clobbers a translate(-50%,-50%) centre (wobble).
5. **Layout:** invented stat rows (`10k+ users`, `99.9% uptime`, `24/7`),
   `01/02/03` markers on unordered sections, cards nested in cards, one
   spacing value stamped everywhere (`gap-4`/`space-y-4` × N).

## Quality floor

- Lead with the point when the setup adds nothing.
- Specific beats punchy: names, numbers, dates, mechanisms, consequences.
- Portability test: if a sentence could move to any other product unchanged,
  it is filler — cut it or make it specific.
- Active voice with human subjects. The team shipped it Tuesday beats the
  decision emerged.
- Show, don't tell. No "this highlights our commitment to".
- One accent, one voice. Subtract first.
- Preserve the user's deliberate choices (brand tokens, a logo, a real
  illustration) — that is what separates taste from slop.

